.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- remove empty colon-path directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I DIRECTORY
\&...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
removes empty directories given as colon-paths.
For
.BR BASE:LEAF ,
it removes the physical path
.B BASE/LEAF
and then empty parents along
.I LEAF
(deepest first), stopping at
.BR BASE .
Only empty directories are removed.
.PP
Plain (non-colon) arguments are passed to
.BR rmdir (1).
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a/b:d/e/f
Removes empty
.BR a/b/d/e/f ,
then empty
.B a/b/d/e
and
.B a/b/d
if possible.
Leaves
.B a/b
in place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the planned
.B rmdir
steps without executing them.
.PP
Options for plain operands are passed through to
.BR rmdir (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (1),
.BR colon-rm (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
